![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `buildSummary` function destructures `procedureInstances`, `procedureStepInstances`, and `reviewTasks` but does not verify if they are valid arrays. If any of these properties are missing or null, it will throw a `TypeError` during iteration or filtering.

Please use `Array.isArray` to safely default to empty arrays, preventing runtime crashes.

```javascript
function buildSummary({
  pilot,
  validator,
  procedureInstances,
  procedureStepInstances,
  reviewTasks,
  generatedAt,
}) {
  procedureInstances = Array.isArray(procedureInstances) ? procedureInstances : [];
  procedureStepInstances = Array.isArray(procedureStepInstances) ? procedureStepInstances : [];
  reviewTasks = Array.isArray(reviewTasks) ? reviewTasks : [];
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When dereferencing and mapping properties from potentially missing or malformed input artifacts, use Array.isArray to safely default to an empty array if the property is not an array, preventing TypeErrors.
</details>

